  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "r0b0tlab's native Blackwell benchmark serve of the official DeepSeek V4 Flash checkpoint on two GB10 Sparks: prebuilt vLLM (dda4668b, torch 2.11 cu130) image, tensor parallel 2 with expert parallel over RoCE, fp8 KV cache, DeepGEMM block-scaled FP8 and MXFP4 MoE, MTP speculative decoding with 2 tokens, FULL_AND_PIECEWISE CUDA graphs. Upstream latency profile by default: 200,000 token context, 2 sequences, 4096 batched tokens, 0.85 memory utilization (its throughput profile is 65,536 context, 16 sequences, 8192 batched tokens). Upstream's optional DeepGEMM SM121 and MoE-padding mods are not applied. The upstream repository declares no licence file; the model is MIT (information only). Upstream reports 38 tok/s at c=1 on driver 580.142 and a throughput regression on driver 580.159; figures are upstream claims. The model revision is not named upstream and is pinned to the newest one at its benchmark date.",
    "tags": [
      "candidate",
      "deepseek",
      "distributed",
      "executable",
      "mtp",
      "openai",
      "r0b0tlab",
      "spark",
      "vllm"
    ],
    "title": "DeepSeek V4 Flash FP8 vLLM dual Spark (r0b0tlab)"
  },
